  "id": "COMPOUND:24565 - PROTEIN:5677",
  "verbalization": "Marsdenoside K appears to have a shared target relationship with JM1 through a series of intermediate molecules, all of which are involved in the regulation of cellular processes. The evidence suggests that Marsdenoside K acts as a target for VMRC-LCP, which in turn is targeted by Glycitein and another compound, (5R,7S,8S)-5-hydroxy-4-methoxy-7,8-dimethyl-7,8-dihydro-5H-pyrano[4,3-b]pyran-2-one. These compounds are all implicated in the modulation of cellular pathways, and their targeting by Marsdenoside K may lead to a downstream effect on JM1. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential mechanism where Marsdenoside K influences JM1 through a series of molecular interactions, possibly by modulating the activity of these intermediates. The evidence supports a plausible, though not yet fully elucidated, mechanism by which Marsdenoside K exerts its biological effects on JM1.",
